course: dictionary
lesson: 12919
title: Etched
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Etched means cut or scratched into a hard surface, like glass, metal or stone, to make a picture or words. «The artist etched a tiny fox into the copper plate.» The fox was not painted on. It was cut into the metal.
explain: The word can also describe something you can see or remember clearly. If a sight or a feeling is etched on your face or your memory, it stays there and does not go away. «Worry was etched on his face» means you could easily see that he was worried.
explain: Look for context clues. Words like glass, metal, stone or silver tell you the word is about cutting into a hard surface. Words like face, memory or forever tell you it means something stays clearly in your mind or on your face.
fact: Etched means cut or scratched into a hard surface such as glass, metal or stone.
fact: Etching can be done with acid or with a sharp tool.
fact: In art, etching is a printmaking method: a picture is cut into a metal plate, then printed onto paper.
fact: «Worry was etched on his face» means the worry was clear to see and did not fade away.
fact: «That day is etched in my memory» means you will remember it clearly for a long time.
exercise: «The window was etched with tiny flowers.» What does etched mean here? | Washed clean by the rain | Broken into many pieces | Painted on with bright colours | *Cut or scratched into the glass to make a picture
exercise: «Her sad face was etched with worry.» What does etched suggest? | Worry was quickly hidden away | She was singing a happy song | *Worry showed clearly and stayed there | She had just woken up from a nap
exercise: «The name was etched into the silver ring.» Find and copy the word that means cut into the metal. | ring | name | *etched | silver
test: Tom says, «That day is etched in my memory.» What does he mean? | He forgot the day completely | *It is a day he will remember clearly for a long time | It was a day with lots of rain
test: Which of these is an example of etching? | A picture drawn in chalk on a pavement | *A picture cut into a metal plate, then printed onto paper | A picture made of sand dropped on a beach | A picture painted with a brush on paper
exam: «The old bridge had words etched into its stone.» What does etched mean here? | Dropped into the river | Covered in soft green moss | Painted in bright colours | *Cut or scratched into the stone
